DESCRIPTION Grounding band, a question the catalog has nothing for; the answer says so and names no title, date, or link from memory.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "What has Quillon Vrasmotte published recently on O'Reilly?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

# The catalog has no author by this name, so every search returns nothing. The same
# assertions hold when the catalog cannot be reached (the search tool is missing or every
# call fails): with no catalog results the answer names no item and holds no link.

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

# The coordinator answers that nothing was found, so no specialist agreement is asserted.
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "catalog")

# No link of any kind: there is no catalog item to link to.
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "http" AND "](" AND "oreilly.com/book/" AND "learning.oreilly.com/library/" AND "common knowledge" AND "general knowledge")

ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The answer says plainly that the O'Reilly catalog search found nothing by an author named Quillon Vrasmotte, or that the O'Reilly catalog could not be searched, and stops there. It names no book, video, course, or live event, gives no publication date, edition, or page count, and contains no link. It does not suggest titles from general knowledge, does not guess what the author may have written, and does not reason about today's date to pick titles. It may suggest checking the spelling of the name, without giving a link. (the constant is a short statement that the catalog had nothing, or could not be searched, with no invented titles, dates, or links.)")
